## Recommended Batch 18 Item 2 — checkout page + customer publicProcedure (T2-T3, ~25K)

Customer takes the populated cart → visits /[slug]/store/checkout → fills shipping +
billing + email → submits → backend creates an EcommerceOrder (pending status) +
optionally creates Xendit invoice immediately → redirect to Xendit payment URL.

- Item 2 (T2-T3 ~25K): Checkout page + placeOrderAsCustomer publicProcedure
  • New: `apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/store/checkout/page.tsx` (Server shell —
    look up tenant default warehouse, redirect to /products if empty cart impossible to
    detect server-side, render the Client form).
  • New: `apps/web/src/app/(tenant)/[slug]/store/checkout/checkout-form.tsx` (Client —
    reads cart from useCart hook, fields for name+email+shippingAddress+billingAddress
    + sameAsShipping toggle, submit calls placeOrderAsCustomer.useMutation, onSuccess
    optionally invokes createXenditInvoice and redirects; onError shows sonner toast).
  • Modified: `apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/storefront.ts` (+placeOrderAsCustomer
    publicProcedure — input schema includes tenantSlug to resolve tenant from URL, items
    + addresses + customer-email; resolves OR creates a Customer record by email match,
    creates EcommerceOrder pending paymentStatus, applies same inventory hold logic as
    existing placeOrder writeProcedure).
  • Modified: `apps/web/src/__tests__/storefront.test.ts` (+5-8 tests for
    placeOrderAsCustomer: guest happy path, existing-customer-by-email match,
    empty-items rejection, invalid-product rejection, stock-insufficient rejection,
    XSS sanitization on customer name field).
  • Modified: `apps/web/src/components/cart/cart-drawer.tsx` (replace disabled
    "Checkout (coming soon)" placeholder with active Link to /[slug]/store/checkout).
  • Branch: feat/batch-18-item-2-checkout-public-procedure
  • ⚠ Pre-flight risk to verify at proposal time:
    (a) rate-limit tier confirmation (rateLimiters.public 30/min vs checkout
        submission rate — 30/min is generous; consider whether burst protection
        helps or not for legitimate checkouts).
    (b) Customer model fields — confirm what's required vs optional (email, name,
        phone, shippingAddress, billingAddress); existing placeOrder requires
        customerId so it never creates one, but customer self-checkout needs
        find-or-create-by-email.
    (c) Xendit integration: option (i) Server-side immediately call
        createXenditInvoice inside placeOrderAsCustomer transaction (one round-trip,
        cleaner UX); option (ii) Return orderId, let client call createXenditInvoice
        separately (two round-trips, simpler error recovery). Pick at proposal time.
    (d) Guest checkout vs require-login: spec at proposal time. If guest: no auth
        gate on placeOrderAsCustomer. If require-login: convert to protectedProcedure
        and skip this batch's first-publicProcedure framing.

